WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.740
- I have to say, congrats.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.831
You were just inducted into
the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:00:03.831 --> 00:00:04.692
- I know.

00:00:04.692 --> 00:00:06.882
(audience cheers)

00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:07.922
- I wanna see, can I see it?

00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:08.755
- I know.

00:00:08.755 --> 00:00:10.200
I brought this for the show.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.880
This is my Rock and Roll

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.580
and I just wanna share this
with you until you get your own,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.413
and you will.

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:16.623
- Oh, I will not, but I love you.

00:00:16.623 --> 00:00:18.690
- You will, you will, you will.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.523
- You are so,

00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:20.520
I think you have to,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.253
well it's funny, I was
literally talking to

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:24.750
my producer this morning and I was like,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.820
we throw around the word icon a lot.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.710
Like I feel like everybody's an icon now.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.270
Like, you know, everybody's
like, oh, she's an icon.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.500
I'm like, no, you have to earn that.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.360
And you actually earned that.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.560
And it's like you, that's
why I loved your response.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.020
I loved your response 'cause
you were like, well wait what?

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:40.853
Rock and roll?

00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:41.686
Like, I'm country music.

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:42.660
But you are rock and roll.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.250
The fact that you're a pioneer for women,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.720
you've opened the doors for so many of us

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.362
to be able to be
vulnerable as songwriters.

00:00:47.362 --> 00:00:48.900
But I don't know, does it make,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.790
does it weird you out
to be labeled an icon?

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.623
Does it, is it?

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:53.573
- Well, I always think of
myself more as an eyesore

00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:54.723
than an icon.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.543
- Well, I wish.

00:00:56.543 --> 00:00:58.202
- Not actually, but you know,

00:00:58.202 --> 00:01:00.750
I used to think when I was young,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.384
if I made it like I'd hoped I would,

00:01:02.384 --> 00:01:05.100
how people would remember
me when I was older.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.730
Now I'm older, and it's
really nice to look back

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.990
and think that, you know,

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.270
I might have done something
that's helped inspire.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.260
- Oh my God, so many things.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.093
- You know, some other people.

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:17.100
And when I got into the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.382
or when they talked about that,

00:01:18.382 --> 00:01:20.370
I didn't realize that it was,

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.570
it was more than just that.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.670
To me, I'd always thought
about the Rock and Roll

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.740
Hall of Fame being for
people that spend their life

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.140
in rock music, like country music.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.430
I mean, you don't see Led Zeppelin

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.320
in the Country Music Hall of Fame.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.600
You know, so I, when they first said that,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.210
I thought, well, you know, I
don't know that I belong there

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.010
and I didn't wanna take
votes from other people

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.030
that spent their life.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.020
And that's kinda how I felt.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.054
- [Kelly] That is so Dolly.

00:01:41.054 --> 00:01:42.300
Who says that?

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.340
- [Dolly] But still, I
honestly thought that,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.950
but then later I saw that
it was for people also

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.669
that have, you know,
influenced other people.

00:01:48.669 --> 00:01:51.810
And I did say I would accept
it gracefully and humbly,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:52.740
and I did.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.060
And I was very honored.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.050
But-

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.370
- But you did something even cooler.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.593
You actually wrote like
a rock and roll song.

00:01:58.593 --> 00:01:59.426
- I did.

00:01:59.426 --> 00:02:00.259
I wrote a song for the show

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:01.800
about my whole experience about that.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.050
It's called, I've been,
it's called Rocking It.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:04.890
'Cause I've been rocking it.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.750
I grew up lovin' Elvis and,

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.149
wild man Jerry Lee, Chuck
Berry, Little Richard,

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:12.120
they had all cast a spell on me,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.790
and Carl Perkins and them Blue Suede Shoes

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.470
had no place on the farm.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.910
There's better than them Brogans

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.850
I was wearing around the barn.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.020
So I've been rocking, rocking, rocking

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.150
since the day I was born.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.690
I'll be rocking till the day I'm gone.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:31.260
'Cause I've got rock and
roll down in my country soul

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:34.408
and I'll be rocking it
till the cows come home.

00:02:34.408 --> 00:02:37.329
(audience cheers)

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:38.482
- That's so perfect.

00:02:38.482 --> 00:02:41.700
- I go ahead and I talk
about the whole thing.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.871
How, you know, how they, you know,

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.760
they put me in the hall of fame

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.260
so I guess it ain't no shame where I said,

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.060
you know but since I heard the big news,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.320
I ain't never been the same.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.360
'Cause they done gone and put me in

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.350
the Rock and Roll Hall of
Fame, it's the dangdest thing.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.960
But I was honored, and I'm proud. So.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.000
- Yeah. And it's so cool
though, how, how you do,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.740
you're so respectful of other artists,

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.573
and all their hard work,

00:03:02.573 --> 00:03:03.810
but at the same time you're like,

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.841
'cause you're doing an album
now, like a rock album.

00:03:05.841 --> 00:03:06.674
- I'm doin' a rock album.

00:03:06.674 --> 00:03:09.052
I'm callin' it Rockstar.

00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:10.383
Rockstar.

00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:11.216
- I love it.

00:03:11.216 --> 00:03:12.372
- A fun, tongue in cheek.

00:03:12.372 --> 00:03:13.205
But I'm actually,

00:03:13.205 --> 00:03:15.120
I'm doing classic songs and I'm usin'

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.130
a lot of the classic artists too,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.140
to sing on some of the songs with me.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:19.973
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:19.973 --> 00:03:21.240
- So I'm looking forward to that.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.990
So that's gonna come out next year.

